 "summary": "A single 20 V Schottky rectifier rated 0.5 A average, in the two-lead SOD-123 surface-mount case. Forward drop is at most 0.385 V at 0.5 A and 25 °C, and a guard ring protects the junction against stress. Uses named are low-voltage high-frequency rectification, freewheeling and reverse-polarity protection. The SBR8 versions are the automotive build, AEC-Q101 qualified and PPAP capable, with site and change control.",
